Project Monitoring System (PMS) - Simple README

1) What this project is
- A desktop app to plan, assign and track project work.
- Roles: Project Manager, Team Leader, Team Member, Senior Employee.
- Shows dashboards, team progress, tasks and reports.
- New: Team Member can view colleagues’ progress under the same Team Leader (Team Overview tab).

2) How to run
- Requirements: Python 3.10+ installed.
- Install dependency: pip install -r requirements.txt
- Start the app: python login.py
- Default admin login:
  - Username: admin
  - Password: admin

3) First run behavior
- The app creates employee.db automatically.
- Seed data (sample projects, members, tasks) is added for demo.

4) Quick role guide
- Admin / Project Manager: create projects, manage tasks, view reports.
- Team Leader: assign tasks, view team stats and urgent alerts.
- Team Member: see own tasks, log time, mark attendance, view Team Overview.
- Senior Employee: read-only access to dashboards and reports.

5) Main screens
- Dashboard: key numbers and deadlines.
- Projects: list, status and progress.
- Tasks: assign, update and track.
- Employee Panel (Team Member):
  - Dashboard, Tasks, Team Overview, My History, Ask Query, Attendance, Timesheets.

6) Optional local API (for HTTP access)
- Start: python api.py
- Test: http://localhost:5000/
- Examples:
  - /api/projects
  - /api/tasks
  - /api/stats/summary

7) Files you may open
- login.py  → starts the app.
- project_monitor.py → main UI and logic.
- api.py → optional Flask API.
- employee.db → SQLite database file (auto-created).
- USER_MANUAL.md → detailed step-by-step user guide.
- README.md → longer, PPT-ready explanation.

8) Troubleshooting
- If no window appears, run from a terminal: python login.py
- Make sure Python is installed and added to PATH.
- If database errors show, delete employee.db to recreate (only if you don’t need existing data).
- On Windows, some antivirus may block GUI apps. Allow Python if prompted.

9) Security note
- Passwords are stored using SHA-256 hashing.
- All data is local to this computer (SQLite).

10) Demo tips
- Log in with admin/admin to explore all features.
- For Team Member view, use any sample employee name that exists in employee.db.

Enjoy using PMS!
